@page
@model Project_R_._8.Pages.cshtml.RulesModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Tutorial";
}

<h1>🏆 Leaderboard Validation Rules</h1>
<p>
    Only runs that follow all rules below will be accepted onto the leaderboard.
    Any violation will result in the run being invalidated.
</p>
<section class="leaderboard-rules">
    <ol>
        <li>
            <strong>Checkpoint Order</strong><br>
            All checkpoints must be passed in the correct order.
            Skipping, reversing, or missing a checkpoint will invalidate the run.
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>Track Limits</strong><br>
            Leaving the track for more than the allowed time limit is not permitted.
            Using off-track areas to gain an advantage will invalidate the run.
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>Respawn Abuse</strong><br>
            Excessive use of reset or respawn features is not allowed.
            Respawning to gain time or position advantages will invalidate the run.
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>Time Manipulation</strong><br>
            Runs are invalid if the browser tab loses focus, the page is refreshed,
            developer tools are opened, or system time is modified during the run.
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>Speed and Physics Integrity</strong><br>
            Modifying game speed, physics values, collision behavior,
            or movement limits will invalidate the run.
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>Pause Exploitation</strong><br>
            Pausing the game or minimizing the browser during a leaderboard run
            will invalidate the run.
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>Automated Inputs</strong><br>
            The use of macros, scripts, bots, or automated input tools is not allowed.
            Input patterns must reflect normal human behavior.
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>Power-Up Restrictions</strong><br>
            Power-ups are disabled in leaderboard mode unless explicitly stated.
            Using any restricted power-up will invalidate the run.
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>Debug and Developer Modes</strong><br>
            Runs completed with debug features, developer tools,
            or test modes enabled will not be accepted.
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>Game Version Consistency</strong><br>
            Runs must be completed on the current official game version.
            Runs from outdated or modified versions are invalid.
        </li>
    </ol>
</section>